Gears of War 3: speckle and off colours at 2x internal resolution, part 2. The colour grading table
(rendered into a 16-pixel wide target, read as a 16x16x16 3D texture) must be filtered at 1x: a
resolution-scaled copy (each entry a 2x2 block of host pixels) bands or bleeds in the final pass.
With resolution scaling, resolves whose destination pitch is at most gpu_unscaled_resolve_max_pitch
pixels (default 32, hot reload, 0 = off) are also downscaled into shared memory, and the range is
unmarked as scaled, so textures are made from the 1x copy. With 0058 every host pixel of the pass
holds the 1x value, so the downscale is exact. The downscale is a new shader,
resolve_downscale_units.cs.hlsl (32bpp and 64bpp), following the scaled layout the resolve shaders
write (16-byte guest units stored as scale_x * scale_y host sub-units, column-major);
resolve_downscale.cs.hlsl assumes one contiguous block per pixel, which that layout is not (its
readback output is scrambled the same way). Compiled with fxc /T cs_5_1 /E main
/Vn resolve_downscale_units_cs. Confirmed at 2x; 3x still shows wrong colours (open issue).

